jq("j-c-custom-thread-pool", "Your Own Thread Pool", "HARD", T, "Write a tiny pool: `w` worker threads take `Runnable` tasks from a `LinkedBlockingQueue`. Submit `n` tasks where task `i` stores `i * i` into slot `i` of a result array, then shut the pool down (send one stop signal per worker) and wait. Print `Result <i>: <value>` for `i = 1..n`.", "One line: `w n`.", "`n` lines.", "1 <= w <= 4, 1 <= n <= 30",
   'MiniPool pool = new MiniPool(w);\nint[] result = new int[n + 1];\nfor (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n    final int x = i;\n    pool.submit(() -> result[x] = x * x);\n}\npool.shutdownAndWait();\nfor (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) System.out.println("Result " + i + ": " + result[i]);', ["2 5", "1 3", "4 10", "3 1", "2 30"], [("int", "w n")], imports="java.util.concurrent.*",
   classes='class MiniPool {\n    private static final Runnable STOP = () -> {\n    };\n    private final BlockingQueue<Runnable> queue = new LinkedBlockingQueue<>();\n    private final Thread[] workers;\n    MiniPool(int n) {\n        workers = new Thread[n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            workers[i] = new Thread(() -> {\n                try {\n                    while (true) {\n                        Runnable task = queue.take();\n                        if (task == STOP) return;\n                        task.run();\n                    }\n                } catch (InterruptedException e) {\n                }\n            });\n            workers[i].start();\n        }\n    }\n    void submit(Runnable r) {\n        queue.add(r);\n    }\n    void shutdownAndWait() throws InterruptedException {\n        for (int i = 0; i < workers.length; i++) queue.add(STOP);\n        for (Thread t : workers) t.join();\n    }\n}')
jq("j-c-bank-transfer", "Safe Bank Transfers", "HARD", T, "Two accounts start with `a` and `b` rupees. Thread 1 moves 1 rupee from account 1 to account 2, `m` times; thread 2 moves 1 rupee from account 2 to account 1, `m` times. To avoid a deadlock both threads always lock the account with the **smaller id** first. Print `Account 1: <x>` and `Account 2: <y>` (the balances never go negative in the tests).", "One line: `a b m`.", "Two lines.", "a, b >= m",
   'Acct x = new Acct(1, a), y = new Acct(2, b);\nThread t1 = new Thread(() -> {\n    for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) Acct.transfer(x, y, 1);\n});\nThread t2 = new Thread(() -> {\n    for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) Acct.transfer(y, x, 1);\n});\nt1.start();\nt2.start();\nt1.join();\nt2.join();\nSystem.out.println("Account 1: " + x.balance);\nSystem.out.println("Account 2: " + y.balance);', ["100 100 50", "10 10 10", "1000 500 500", "5 5 1", "300 200 200"], [("int", "a b m")],
   classes='class Acct {\n    final int id;\n    int balance;\n    Acct(int id, int balance) {\n        this.id = id;\n        this.balance = balance;\n    }\n    static void transfer(Acct from, Acct to, int amount) {\n        Acct first = from.id < to.id ? from : to, second = first == from ? to : from;\n        synchronized (first) {\n            synchronized (second) {\n                from.balance -= amount;\n                to.balance += amount;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}')
jq("j-c-parallel-primes", "Counting Primes with Worker Threads", "MEDIUM", T, "Count the primes up to `n` with `w` worker threads: worker `k` checks the numbers `i` (from 2) with `i % w == k`, adding to its own count. Print `Primes up to <n>: <total>` after joining.", "One line: `w n`.", "One line.", "1 <= w <= 6, 2 <= n <= 100000",
   'int[] part = new int[w];\nThread[] ts = new Thread[w];\nfor (int k = 0; k < w; k++) {\n    final int id = k;\n    ts[k] = new Thread(() -> {\n        for (int i = 2; i <= n; i++) {\n            if (i % w != id) continue;\n            boolean prime = true;\n            for (int d = 2; (long) d * d <= i; d++) if (i % d == 0) { prime = false; break; }\n            if (prime) part[id]++;\n        }\n    });\n    ts[k].start();\n}\nfor (Thread t : ts) t.join();\nint total = 0;\nfor (int c : part) total += c;\nSystem.out.println("Primes up to " + n + ": " + total);', ["2 100", "1 2", "4 1000", "3 10", "6 100000"], [("int", "w n")])
jq("j-c-worker-queue", "A Worker Thread with a Queue", "MEDIUM", T, "One worker thread takes numbers from a `BlockingQueue`, squares them and appends the result to a list, until it takes the stop value `-1`. Put `n` numbers and then `-1` in the queue and print the results (in order) on one line after the worker ends.", "First line `n`, then `n` non-negative integers.", "The squares.", "1 <= n <= 100",
   'BlockingQueue<Integer> q = new LinkedBlockingQueue<>();\nList<Integer> out = new ArrayList<>();\nThread worker = new Thread(() -> {\n    try {\n        int x;\n        while ((x = q.take()) != -1) out.add(x * x);\n    } catch (InterruptedException e) {\n    }\n});\nworker.start();\nfor (int x : a) q.put(x);\nq.put(-1);\nworker.join();\nSystem.out.println(out.toString().replaceAll("[\\\\[\\\\],]", ""));', [arr([1, 2, 3]), arr([5]), arr([0, 4]), arr([10, 20, 30, 40]), arr([7, 7])], [("arr", "n a")], imports="java.util.concurrent.*")
jq("j-c-fork-join", "ForkJoinPool", "HARD", T, "Add up `n` numbers with a `RecursiveTask<Long>`: a task for more than 4 numbers splits its range in two halves (`fork` one, `compute` the other, then `join`); small ranges are added directly. Run it in a `ForkJoinPool` and print `Sum: <total>`.", "First line `n`, then `n` integers.", "One line.", "1 <= n <= 1000",
   'long total = new ForkJoinPool().invoke(new SumTask(a, 0, n));\nSystem.out.println("Sum: " + total);', [arr([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8]), arr([5]), arr([10, 20, 30]), arr(list(range(1, 21))), arr([-5, 5, -10, 10, 7])], [("arr", "n a")], imports="java.util.concurrent.*",
   classes='class SumTask extends RecursiveTask<Long> {\n    private final int[] a;\n    private final int lo, hi;\n    SumTask(int[] a, int lo, int hi) {\n        this.a = a;\n        this.lo = lo;\n        this.hi = hi;\n    }\n    protected Long compute() {\n        if (hi - lo <= 4) {\n            long s = 0;\n            for (int i = lo; i < hi; i++) s += a[i];\n            return s;\n        }\n        int mid = (lo + hi) / 2;\n        SumTask left = new SumTask(a, lo, mid), right = new SumTask(a, mid, hi);\n        left.fork();\n        return right.compute() + left.join();\n    }\n}')
jq("j-c-parallel-merge-sort", "Parallel Merge Sort", "HARD", T, "Sort `n` numbers with a `RecursiveTask`: split the array in halves, sort each half in its own task (`fork` and `compute`), then merge the two sorted halves. Print the sorted numbers on one line.", "First line `n`, then `n` integers.", "The sorted array.", "1 <= n <= 1000",
   'int[] sorted = new ForkJoinPool().invoke(new SortTask(a));\nStringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\nfor (int i = 0; i < sorted.length; i++) sb.append(sorted[i]).append(i < sorted.length - 1 ? " " : "");\nSystem.out.println(sb);', [arr([5, 2, 9, 1]), arr([7]), arr([3, 3, 1]), arr([5, 4, 3, 2, 1]), arr([-1, 5, -3, 2, 0, 8])], [("arr", "n a")], imports="java.util.concurrent.*",
   classes='class SortTask extends RecursiveTask<int[]> {\n    private final int[] a;\n    SortTask(int[] a) {\n        this.a = a;\n    }\n    protected int[] compute() {\n        if (a.length <= 1) return a;\n        int mid = a.length / 2;\n        SortTask left = new SortTask(Arrays.copyOfRange(a, 0, mid)), right = new SortTask(Arrays.copyOfRange(a, mid, a.length));\n        left.fork();\n        int[] r = right.compute(), l = left.join();\n        int[] out = new int[a.length];\n        int i = 0, j = 0, k = 0;\n        while (i < l.length && j < r.length) out[k++] = l[i] <= r[j] ? l[i++] : r[j++];\n        while (i < l.length) out[k++] = l[i++];\n        while (j < r.length) out[k++] = r[j++];\n        return out;\n    }\n}')
jq("j-c-traffic-intersection", "A Traffic Intersection", "HARD", T, "Two threads, `North-South` and `East-West`, share an intersection and must take turns: North-South goes first. Each prints `<name> passes` when it is its turn, then hands over. They do this `n` times each. Use `wait()` and `notifyAll()` with a shared `turn` flag so the lines strictly alternate. After joining print `Cycles: <n>`.", ONE, "`2n` alternating lines then a total.", "1 <= n <= 20",
   'Light light = new Light();\nThread ns = new Thread(() -> {\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) light.pass(0, "North-South");\n});\nThread ew = new Thread(() -> {\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) light.pass(1, "East-West");\n});\nns.start();\new.start();\nns.join();\new.join();\nSystem.out.println("Cycles: " + n);', ["2", "1", "5", "10", "3"], JN,
   classes='class Light {\n    private int turn = 0;\n    synchronized void pass(int who, String name) {\n        while (turn != who) {\n            try {\n                wait();\n            } catch (InterruptedException e) {\n                return;\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(name + " passes");\n        turn = 1 - turn;\n        notifyAll();\n    }\n}')
